==Strategy==
Dogumaru, the main threat of this stage, has rather slow attack speed, which makes it possible to sneak in [[:Category:Rusher-class Cats|Rusher-class Cats]] like [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]] or [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Maglev Cat]].

Once hit by Dogumaru, a unit is effectively Cursed forever, since the effect lasts twenty seconds while Dogumaru attacks every 2.87 seconds.

*[[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Slapstick Cats]], being strong against Relics and immune to Curse, can work very well against Dogumaru, dealing heavy damage and being able to take a few hits. They work even better with [[Talents]], and are able to Weaken Dogumaru in the best of cases, removing pressure from both themselves and other meatshields.
*[[Idi:N (Special Cat)|Idi:N2]] is also amazing, as she can rush Dogumaru and deal enough damage to three or four shot it. Due to Dogumaru's relatively low damage, Idi may get multiple attacks in, potentially crippling if not destroying Dogumaru in a single attempt. However, timing is absolutely essential, as Dogumaru spawns up to three times in this stage, so you need to make the most out of each Idi you spawn, and have other options ready. On higher difficulties, Idi might not be as useful as Dogumaru becomes too durable for Idi to kill, but it would still be wise to have around just in case, especially if you have her True Form.
*[[Elder Beast Naala (Special Cat)|Awakened Naala]] can be a phenomenal unit to use in the crowned difficulties, as they are strong against Relics and curse immune, despite being outranged by Dogumaru. They can tank a fair bit from him, and their reliable weaken can easily cripple Dogumaru's pushing power.
*[[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Doron]] is incredibly useful due to his anti-Relic freeze (and knockback in true form), giving your other units time to deal damage to Dogumaru and regain lost ground. This makes him an essential choice for 2-crown or above. If you're lucky enough, the Surge left from Doron's attack can also deal with any peons that may be in the way or extend his freeze duration further.
*[[Mecha-Bun (Special Cat)|Ultimate Mecha-Bun]] does okay against Dogumaru, inflicting a solid 12,750 damage per hit and having 136,000 health at level 30. As long as there are no Dark Otters around, Mecha-Bun could be used to great effect. However, there are many other better options to use, meaning he's usually a last resort, such as when you lack better units. If in need of a tank for higher crown difficulties, you can use (ironically) [[Dogumaru (Special Cat)|Reborn Warrior Doguemon]], who can resist Relics and does decent generalist damage.

Before attempting Primitive Souls, it is HIGHLY recommended to boost your cats up to level 40 at the VERY minimum, but ideally to level 50. Level 30s will not be enough on this stage. Levels are especially important on [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]], as below level 53 (Level 48 with an Attack Up (Sm) [[Cat Combo]]), Fishman Cat cannot 2HKO the starting Mooths. You'll end up wasting your time and funds trying to kill it instead of getting free money from them, which matters the most on how the rest of your response will fare against them.

This stage plays out very similarly to [[Draconian (Deadly)|Draconian]]. Both have Mooths at the start of the stage, both have waves of otters to support the main boss (Dark Otters in this case), and their main threats spawn in trios. Even Dogumaru and [[Manic King Dragon (Enemy)|Manic King Dragon]] fill very similar roles in battle, being low DPS units with high health and extreme range meant to gradually chip and destroy your units.

However, the strategy for this stage is different from Draconian. The general idea is to destroy the Mooths and the first Dark Otter quickly, then damage the first Dogumaru while it's approaching. After that, 2 Dark Otters come and you kill them and then finish off the first Dogumaru right before the second Dogumaru approaches. Then damage the second Dogumaru just like the first one, and you'll see two more Dark Otters and the third and final Dogumaru approaching. Destroy the Dark Otters and finish off the second Dogumaru. Then destroy the third Dogumaru and finish the stage. The key to victory is to kill each Dogumaru before the next comes, or their repeated attacks will stunlock your units without help from something like Doron to disable them.

Because there are fewer Dogumarus than Manic King Dragon Cats, however, there's a noticeable delay. The first spawns 46.7 seconds in, the second 106.7 seconds in, and the third 173.3 seconds in. Because the first takes 46.7 seconds to arrive, with the appropriate units, the stage can be rushed and potentially beaten before Dogumaru can even spawn.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
The following [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rares]] are good for this stage, and if you have any of these, using them will make things easier.
*[[Tecoluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Lufalan Pasalan]]: Outranges Dogumaru's Omni-Strike and provides support against Dark Otters. Be careful with him, since he has single target, only stands outside by 20 distance and any shift in the frontline will destroy him.
*[[Lesser Demon Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Greater Balrog Cat]]: With maxed ATK and Strengthen Talents, once his Strengthen activates, he has a mind-boggling 131,028 DPS at level 40, along with lightning-fast recharge for an Uber Rare. This allows him to easily melt the bulky units presented here, but his low range and single target can be a problem. He can work without talents to some extent in the lowest difficulty, but you will definitely need his talents for the higher difficulties as his damage won't keep up with the bloated stats the Otters and Dogumarus gain.
*[[Sanada Yukimura (Uber Rare Cat)|Immortal Yukimura]]: Massive damage to Darks, insane speed along with a 1f attack animation, which means he has a near-guaranteed chance to deliver hits, on top of having a short recharge time for you to possibly send more when needed. Can make easy work of the Dark Otters before Dogumaru could curse him if timed well.
*[[Kalisa (Uber Rare Cat)|Divine Kalisa]]: Despite the lack of Angels, her good movement speed, knockback rate, and health allow her to chip a nice amount of Dogumaru's HP, or you can use her to deal damage to the peons instead. [[Twinstars (Uber Rare Cat)|Divine Twinstars Φ]] can be an alternative substitute, since it works similar to her.
*[[Maeda Keiji (Uber Rare Cat)|Immortal Keiji]]: High health and DPS, along with a short recharge time allows him to work as a midranger. He can't be used for tanking, however, as Dogumaru will simply curse him.
*[[Kai (Uber Rare Cat)|Divine Kai μ]]: Can tank a fair amount, even if the Dogumarus are stacked, has a quick recharge allowing for her to get back and soak up more damage, and can dish out some great punishment, but you might reconsider spawning her when there is Dark Otters on the field. [[Baby Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Cats in the Cradle]] can be an alternative substitute, for similar reasons.
*[[The Grateful Crane (Uber Rare Cat)|Ultima Galaxy Cosmo]]: Able to hit Dogumaru while having enough standing range to remain safe from their hits. Also, at level 32 or higher, he deals enough damage to kill the Ginger Snaches in one hit, which helps to prevent them from getting in other units' way. [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]] also works as a substitute, admittedly only as a debuffer. [[Red Riding Mina (Special Cat)|Awakened Mina]] is also great here, as her Long Distance attacks can weaken Dogumaru.
*[[Kasa Jizo (Uber Rare Cat)|Kasa Jizo]]: Great mid-ranged DPS for the Otters and Snaches. [[Baby Gao (Uber Rare Cat)|Baby Gao]] works just as well, but is more effective for the Snaches and less for the Otters. Take care that Dogumaru might shut down their abilities with his curse.
*[[Balaluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Piccolan Pasalan]]: Able to constantly freeze and disrupt Dogumaru's attack in addition to weakening them, allowing shorter-ranged cats, especially rushers like Awakened Bahamut or Ultimate Mecha-Bun, to get in and deal a lot more damage than they normally would.
*[[Saber (Uber Rare Cat)|Saber Alter CC]]: Great DPS and movement speed, and Long Distance makes it less likely that a peon interferes with her and Dogumaru. Knockback resets her attack rate, she's cheap to deploy, and her recharge time makes her very helpful here. [[D'arktanyan (Uber Rare Cat)|Valiant D'arktanyan]] can be alternative substitute, for similar reasons.
*[[Baby Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Cats in the Cradle]]: They have good health, quick recharge time, and they deal a lot of damage + level 2 Wave Attack. The wave greatly helps at it allows them to kill the frontlines quicker and be able to damage Dogumaru even if there's something standing in the way, making them very versatile in here.
*[[Kasli the Scourge (Uber Rare Cat)|Ritual Saint Kasli]]: Her first form is not recommended here, so her second form is the effective bomb. Decent health, immunity to Curse, great offensive and pusher capabilities, that push Dark Otters and Dogumaru back which is extremely useful for regaining standing ground on the fight. Be careful as Kasli has 5 KB and 50K HP which means she will die quickly if you do not put in consideration when you spawn her.
*[[Hades the Punisher (Uber Rare Cat)|Almighty Hades]]: He can tank many attacks from Dogumaru and his quick attack rate can kill the Ginger Snaches if they interfere, but might die quickly from the Dark Otters. Beware his higher-than-usual recharge time.
*[[Lasvoss (Uber Rare Cat)|Lasvoss Reborn]]: He has high health at level 40, more consistent at level 50, and can 1 shot Dark Otters if he performs a savage blow. He can sneak up on Dogumaru and remove over 50-75% of his health, as long as Ginger Snaches don't get in the way.
*[[Trixi the Merc (Uber Rare Cat)|Trixi the Revenant]]: Very powerful crowd-controller against Dogumaru, and pairs well with other rushers thanks to her Freeze.
*[[Daybreaker Izanagi (Legend Rare Cat)|Dawnbringer Izanagi]]: Not only wlll he able to tank attacks from Dogumaru, but he'll also deal a crippling amount of damage. Izanagi will be able to clear the ginger snaches with his summon, allowing an easier time to attack Dogumaru or the Dark otters. In extreme cases; you might be able to rush the base after the first Dogumaru gets defeated by Izanagi.
*[[Child of Destiny Phono (Uber Rare Cat)|King of Destiny Phonoa]]: Extremely high DPS against traited enemies, and can easily snipe the Dogumarus provided there's a stepping stone in the way.
*[[Celestial Child Luna (Uber Rare Cat) |Salvation's Daughter Lunacia]]: Her explosion along with her freezes excels in damaging and chipping Dogumarus. She could also tank serious damage from Dogumarus, giving you a much easier time to deal with them. Make sure to deal with the  otters, though.
*[[Squire Luno (Uber Rare Cat)|Lunos the Luminous]]: His Conjure and cooldown, combined with his damage and health, makes the stage trivial. Lunos can to knock back and chip down Dogamarus while tanking hits from enemies with ease. He can also take down the Dark otters and Ginger Snaches.

